    obs(OBS-OB-002): emit gate/scheduler health metrics on /metrics/prom
    
    Ships spec §3.2's five Tier-2 families: obo_cron_ticks_total{outcome},
    obo_cron_skip_reason_total{reason}, obo_host_load1, obo_host_mem_used_fraction,
    obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds. Both label sets are CLOSED and
    pre-initialised at 0 so rate() has a series before the first tick/skip; the three
    gauges are omitted (never NaN, never a fabricated 0) until a reading exists. Tick
    stamps at the TOP of Tick and settles exactly one outcome on every return path
    (idle_gated for IdleGateError before returning, empty, solved, error).
    
    Label reconciliation vs the board row: the row's provisional `deferred`/`attempted`
    are NOT what shipped — spec §3.2 is design authority, so the closed outcome set is
    solved|empty|idle_gated|error (row `deferred` -> spec `idle_gated`, row `attempted`
    -> spec `solved`). Reason vocabulary is TrimSpaceReason's load|memory|load+memory;
    an unrecognised reason is dropped rather than widening the label set. Spec §3.2
    needed no edit: names/types/labels shipped exactly as written.
    
    Live numbers (scratch :18766, -cron-interval 2s -load-threshold 0.1, host load1 ~20):
    obo_host_load1 20.41 vs /proc/loadavg 20.41, then 20.61 vs 20.61 six seconds later
    (0% delta, AC2's 5% bound). Across that same 6s gap: last_tick 1794867711.37 ->
    1794867717.38, skip_reason{load} 7 -> 10, ticks{idle_gated} 7 -> 10. Scratch :18768
    with -load-threshold -1 (gate open, empty queue): ticks{empty} 7 -> 10 while
    idle_gated stayed 0. Live unit on :8766 untouched (health 200 before and after,
    ActiveEnterTimestamp unchanged).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
